  "author": "A Robot",
  "institution": "MTSU",
  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology",
  "estimatedLength": "25 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the structural components of DNA, including sugar-phosphate backbones, nitrogenous bases, and hydrogen bonds, and relate them to the double-helix architecture.",
    "Apply complementary base-pairing rules to infer a complementary DNA strand and distinguish A-T from G-C pairing by hydrogen-bond number.",
    "Explain how 5' to 3' backbone directionality produces antiparallel DNA strands.",
    "Trace the roles of helicase, single-strand binding proteins, DNA polymerase, and DNA ligase during DNA replication.",
    "Relate antiparallel structure and 5' to 3' polymerase activity to continuous leading-strand and discontinuous lagging-strand synthesis.",
    "Explain why DNA replication is semiconservative and predict the parental and newly synthesized strand composition of daughter DNA molecules."
  ],
