          ],
          "changeMeaning": "The full DNA model is introduced as the anchor object so students first perceive DNA as a three-dimensional double helix rather than as a flat diagram.",
          "narration": "DNA is a double helix made of two long nucleotide strands that twist around a common axis. In this scene, we will examine how its outer backbone, inner bases, and directional strands fit together in three dimensions."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip1",
          "audioClip": "dna_structure_backbones_highlight",
