            },
            {
              "target": "gcPair",
              "enabled": true
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Representative A-T and G-C pairs appear inside the helix so students can connect inward-facing bases with the rungs between the two backbones.",
          "narration": "The nitrogenous bases project inward from each backbone. Across the helix, bases pair specifically: adenine pairs with thymine, and guanine pairs with cytosine."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip3",
