            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Hydrogen-bond markers and a summary label are added to compare the stability of A-T and G-C base pairing without changing the whole scene.",
          "narration": "These base pairs are held together by hydrogen bonds. Adenine and thymine form two hydrogen bonds, while guanine and cytosine form three, making G-C pairs slightly more strongly associated."
        },
