            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "A continuous leading strand and separate Okazaki fragments are revealed to visualize the asymmetry caused by polymerase directionality on antiparallel templates.",
          "narration": "On one template, polymerase can follow the fork continuously, producing the leading strand. On the other template, synthesis occurs discontinuously as short Okazaki fragments that are repeatedly initiated and extended away from the fork."
        },
